Day 71/100 of hashtag#DrGViswanathanChallenge
Today, I solved LeetCode 114 – Flatten Binary Tree to Linked List 
- Approach:

I used preorder traversal to flatten the binary tree in-place.
The main idea is to make the left subtree come before the right subtree, just like preorder: Root - Left - Right.
 Store the current node's left and right children. 
 Connect the previously processed node to the current node using right. 
 Set left = null. 
 Continue recursively through the saved left and right subtrees. 

Time complexity: O(n) 
Space complexity: O(h)

-Key Takeaways:

 1) Preorder traversal is the key to maintaining the required order. 
 2) The tree can be flattened in-place, without creating a separate linked list. 
 3) Saving the original left and right pointers is important before modifying them. 

